Since your frontend is now perfectly wired to call DELETE /JS/voucher/my-requests/by-batch/{batchId}, we just need to ensure your **Java Backend (Spring Boot)** is correctly exposing this API and enforcing the security rules before it triggers the Oracle PURGE_JOURNAL_BATCH procedure.
You do not need to build a massive new architecture, but you must ensure these **two methods** exist and are updated in your backend Controller and Service.
Here is exactly what you should have in your backend to handle the deletion securely and professionally:
### 1. The Controller API Endpoint
Open your VoucherPostingController.java. You need to ensure you have a @DeleteMapping that catches the URL the frontend is calling. It should extract the Maker's User ID from the security token to prevent someone else from deleting their batch.
```java
    /**
     * Maker API: Deletes an entire pending batch that they created.
     */
    @DeleteMapping("/my-requests/by-batch/{batchId}")
    public ResponseEntity<ApiResponseDto> deletePendingBatch(
            @PathVariable String batchId,
            @RequestHeader("Authorization") String token) {
        
        try {
            // Extract the user ID from your JWT/Auth token
            String userId = jwtTokenUtil.extractUserId(token.substring(7)); 
            
            // Send to service layer for validation and deletion
            voucherRequestService.deleteBatchRequest(batchId, userId);
            
            return ResponseEntity.ok(new ApiResponseDto("Success", "Batch deletion process initiated.", null));
        } catch (IllegalStateException e) {
            return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN)
                    .body(new ApiResponseDto("Error", e.getMessage(), null));
        } catch (Exception e) {
            log.error("BATCH_DELETE_FAIL | Batch: {} | Error: {}", batchId, e.getMessage());
            return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR)
                    .body(new ApiResponseDto("Error", "Failed to delete batch", null));
        }
    }

